endobj
168 0 obj
<< /AP << /D 673 0 R /N 674 0 R >> /BS 675 0 R /C [ 0 0 1 ] /CA 0.404999 /Contents (ITEM No. 10 - BLUE ISLAND TRAIN CONNECTION \(ROCK/ELECTRIC\r\rTrain #406 carries a alrge number of commuters weekly who connect with Electric District #502 which departs Blue Island at 7:00 a.m.  Whenever train #406 is running late and there is a question as to whether or not these passengers will make the connection, the conductor will immediately notify Blue Island tower operator advising their expected arrival time at Blue Island.  When so notified, Blue Island Tower will notify the Electric District / Randolph Control at extension 2472 or 2465, advising of the expected arrival time of train #406.  Randolph Control should then advise the tower operator whether they will hold train #502 to pick up the passengers.  The tower operator will then log on the prescribed form the date, time expected to arrive \(from conductor\), name of control operator talked to, and actual arrival time of train #406.  The tower operator will relay to train #406 the response from Randolph Control so that the passengers will be kept informed.) /F 156 /M (D:20090809131006-05'00') /NM (1905de3) /Name /Comment /P 20 0 R /Popup 169 0 R /Rect [ 148.445 283.391 168.446 301.392 ] /Rotate 90 /Subj (Bulletin Notice No. 155) /Subtype /Text /T (RID OPS PRO) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
