<< /AP << /D 796 0 R /N 797 0 R >> /BS 798 0 R /C [ 0 0 1 ] /CA 0.404999 /Contents (WESTWARD TRAINS, BOTH MAINS:\rWhen signal for westwars traffic, located at MP 29.5 indicates a signal more favorable than stop, the engineer must foul the signal circuit with lead trucks of his/her train before crossing gates will activate.  Crossing gates no longer activate automatically when receiving a more favorable signal than stop.  The distance from track1 westward signal to center of Mokena Street is 109 feet.  The distance from track 2 westward signal to the center of Mokena Street is 221 feet.\r\rEASTWARD TRAINS, BOTH MAINS:\rWhen signal for eastward traffic, located at MP 29.5 indicates a signal more favorable than stop, the engineer must foul the signal circuit with lead trucks of his/her train before crossing gates will activate.  Crossing gates no longer activate automatically when receiving a more favorable signal than stop.  The distance from both eastward signals to the center of Wolf Road is 92 feet.) /F 156 /M (D:20090809143906-05'00') /NM (1905e45) /Name /Comment /P 25 0 R /Popup 293 0 R /Rect [ 387.569 427.459 407.57 445.46 ] /Rotate 90 /Subj (Special Instructions Re: Crossings) /Subtype /Text /T (RID OPS PRO) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
